                <pb facs="0809" n="797" sameAs="frus:frus1943v04/pg797"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867N.01/1868: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the United
                        Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-07-09T19:00:00-04:00">July 9, 1943—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4165. Your 4286, June 29, 11 p.m. In as much as it was contemplated that the
                    matter dealt with in the Department’s 3586, June 9, 7 p.m., was to have been
                    considered by the War Cabinet on July 1st, it would be appreciated if the
                    Department might be furnished with a reply as soon as possible.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
